      <data key="d17">paragraph_based_00084</data>
      <data key="d18">The effect of climate change on the frequency and intensity of extreme events can be decomposed into thermodynamic and dynamic effects (Vautard et al. 2016). The thermodynamic effect involves the warming of the atmosphere, directly leading to more extreme heatwaves, less extreme cold spells, and more intense extreme pr</data>
    </edge>
