      <data key="d17">paragraph_based_00364</data>
      <data key="d18">We start our analysis in Fig. 1 by characterizing circulation-induced and residual (thermodynamical) trends of the domain-averaged winter temperature time series over the Germany domain. Dynamical adjustment is a technique in climate science, which aims to estimate the influence of atmospheric circulation on a target s</data>
