      <data key="d17">paragraph_based_00237</data>
      <data key="d18">To assess worst-case-scenario winter temperatures in France, we use the winter of 1962-1963 (hereafter referred to as winter 1963) as a reference event. Winter 1963 yielded an exceptionally low mean temperature anomaly over December, January and February (DJF) of -3.4σ below the seasonal average (Fig. 1a). The year 196</data>
