      <data key="d17">paragraph_based_00064</data>
      <data key="d18">In the NAO-regime, the Azores anticyclone is highly weakened and an anticyclone over Iceland replaces the usual low pressure there. A highly negative NAO index (i.e. a predominant NAO-weather regime) is usually associated with cold winters in Europe (Van Loon and Rogers 1978; Hurrell 1995). For instance, winter of 2009</data>
    </edge>
